<p class="bench-note">Both runtimes snapshot in O(objects) and stay flat as each actor grows larger (17.7 µs for 64-byte actors, 25.4 µs for 16384-byte actors). They share each actor's state instead of copying it. The runtimes differ, so their absolute times are not directly comparable; the shared O(objects) trend is the result. On restore, glowcap frees the rewound copies right away; Goblins leaves that cleanup to its garbage collector.</p>
```

Reproduce the page with `zig build bench-site-report`, or run the individual
commands named in the linked benchmark READMEs.
[What you can depend on]($link.page('stability')) separates in-tree
measurements from outside evidence.
